survey swil2a
#Data from Willie Stanton's Survey Book 1 
# p. 45-46	(=PDF p.49-50)

#Typed in by Footleg, June 2012

#21st July 1951	W.I.Stanton	SWILDONS HOLE
#Swildons 2 Main streamway from near Sump 1 to Creep 2

centreline
cs OSGB:ST 
date 1951.07.21
# Stanton's bearings come out 3 degrees clockwise of the resurvey even after
# the magnetic declination Therion works out for the date. Measured on his
# streamway books (swildons1-c, d and e, 1952-53) against the resurvey there,
# where it is the same for all three; assumed for his other books.
calibrate compass 3    # back bearings too

#in this survey some angles are in degrees:minutes, others decimal degrees
units tape feet
units depth feet

data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
A	B	21	-	103	8:30	A is at the base of the cable spike on the downstream side of Sump I
B	C	27	322:30	-	-9:30	B is on a rock at upstream end of pool
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
C	D	37	-	83	1.5	C is on edge of pool 10' before Duck I
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
D	E	16.2	192:30	-	4:30	D is in stream. Big rock (start of New Series survey) 10' away at 350 (deg). Big passage starts as continuation of Howards Dig.
E	F	47	-	78	-5:30	
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
F	G	48	292	-	-2.5	At 40' the roof lowers suddenly to Creep I. The big Bedding Plane passage comes in on the right, from -5' to 40'
G	H	36	-	159	0	
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
H	I	31	247	-	-2:30	
I	J	26	-	95	2	
J	K	26.5	320	-	1	Pots
K	L	17.5	-	193	-9	Pots
L	M	33	299	-	-3	L is at foot of climb to Approach passage. Clay fill remains 6' up on left wall.
M	N	43	-	142	-7.3	Pots
N	O	15.5	281	-	-2	Pots
O	P	56	-	127	-5	Pots. Very pretty coral on left wall
P	Q	15.8	283	-	-0:15	
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
Q	R	15.3	-	37	-4	1.5 foot deep pool starts at P.
R	S	39.5	310	-	4	Pool 2.5' deep at R, ends 15' on. Scalloping as in Goughs 1st Sandy Chamber.
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
S	T	39.6	-	58	-2:30	S is marked on wall. At 20' there is a muddy chamber overhead.
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
T	U	49	148	-	-1.7	
#	U					Beasts (or Pearls? Not clear in scan) seen here.    Total = 650'
A1	B1	30.4	-	326	0	A1 is far end of "Priddy Green" passage. At choke
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
B1	C1	37.5	248	-	-6:00	B1 is ent to P.G. pass, above stalagmite keloid (sp.?)

endcentreline

endsurvey